From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 13:49:57 +0800
Subject: phy: qcom-qmp-combo: Avoid orientation changes while DP is active

qmp_combo_typec_switch_set() force-cycles the common USB/DP PHY block
when the Type-C orientation changes. During a quick disconnect followed
by a reconnect in the opposite orientation, the new orientation can be
reported before DRM has disabled the previous DP stream.

Restarting the common PHY block while the DP PHY is still powered
invalidates resources used by the active DP link. A later DP link register
access, such as pushing the idle pattern during atomic disable, can then
trigger an asynchronous SError.

Check the applied orientation and dp_powered_on while holding phy_mutex.
Keep the current orientation while the DP PHY is powered so that the
common block is not restarted. A subsequent Type-C notification can apply
the new orientation after the old DP stream has been powered off.

Fixes: 2851117f8f42 ("phy: qcom-qmp-combo: Introduce orientation switching")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>

(cherry picked from commit afb1e8a47a5417da92ee88e792de3a4cb67ae500)
[SuperKali: backported to sc8280xp edge from radxa/kernel linux-7.0.11]
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 12 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4429,10 +4429,18 @@ static int qmp_combo_typec_switch_set(struct typec_switch_dev *sw,
 	struct qmp_combo *qmp = typec_switch_get_drvdata(sw);
 	const struct qmp_phy_cfg *cfg = qmp->cfg;
 
-	if (orientation == qmp->orientation || orientation == TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NONE)
+	if (orientation == TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NONE)
 		return 0;
 
 	mutex_lock(&qmp->phy_mutex);
+
+	/*
+	 * Changing orientation force-cycles the common USB/DP PHY block.
+	 * Defer it until the active DP stream has been powered off.
+	 */
+	if (orientation == qmp->orientation || qmp->dp_powered_on)
+		goto out_unlock;
+
 	qmp->orientation = orientation;
 
 	if (qmp->init_count) {
@@ -4446,6 +4454,8 @@ static int qmp_combo_typec_switch_set(struct typec_switch_dev *sw,
 		if (qmp->dp_init_count)
 			cfg->dp_aux_init(qmp);
 	}
+
+out_unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&qmp->phy_mutex);
 
 	return 0;
-- 
